        "body": "AeroVironment Inc is a public company headquartered in Arlington, Virginia, traded under the ticker AVAV. According to its website, it is a manufacturer of Unmanned Aircraft Systems, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, Loitering Munition Systems, and Unmanned Ground Vehicles used for surveillance and reconnaissance by the United States Military, U.S. allies, and commercial industries. The site also states that the company manufactures High-Altitude Pseudo-Satellites.\n\nThe company describes MacCready Works as its advanced development group, which it says turns concepts into mission-ready autonomous systems. The site says the group's engineers, roboticists, and AI researchers design next-generation robotic systems across air, land, and sea, and that it is inspired by the pioneering spirit of Dr. Paul B. MacCready, Jr. The company describes its approach as the MacCready Method, summarized on the site as build fast, test relentlessly, deploy advantage.\n\nThe company's own site does not list specific AI products in the material reviewed. AeroVironment is recorded with a Virginia law exposure count of 152.",
